<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Rubrics Design</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Below we demonstrate how we designed rubrics for a specific schema, which are subsequently used for retrieving relevant evaluation statements. These rubrics serve as human-validated conceptual preferences that guide LLMs in evaluating submitted database designs against established best practices and theoretical foundations.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A2.F3" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2509.12476v1/figures/sample_erd.png" id="A2.F3.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:558/462;" width="558" height="462" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 3: </span>The schema used for following rubric development</figcaption>
</figure>
